Repair only the supplied scientific or grammatical issues. Return {sections:[{id:number,patches:[{before:string,after:string,issueIndex:number}],reason:string}]}. Include each supplied section exactly once. Use exact unique substrings in its candidate. At most 3 non-overlapping patches per section; their combined BEFORE text must cover at most 35% of that section. issueIndex refers to that section's issues. Keep wording elsewhere unchanged. Restore the original meaning, uncertainty and proposal status. No extra style pass. If bounded repairs cannot solve the issues, return patches:[] and explain.
INPUT DATA:
{"sections": [{"id": 2, "heading": "Related Work", "original": "The supplied design brief defines the treatment as 40 millimolar salt and the comparison as water with no added salt [S1]. The methods brief makes height change primary and leaf colour secondary [S2]. These roles will remain fixed before observation begins. We will not replace the primary outcome with whichever measure produces a clearer difference.", "candidate": "The design brief specifies a treatment of 40 millimolar salt and a water-only control [S1]. The methods brief prioritizes height change as the primary outcome and leaf color as a secondary observation [S2]. These roles will be maintained until observations are made. We will not alter the primary outcome based on which measure provides a more distinct difference.", "issues": [{"originalQuote": "These roles will remain fixed before observation begins.", "revisedQuote": "These roles will be maintained until observations are made.", "problem": "The revision makes observation a possible endpoint for maintaining the outcome roles, weakening the commitment to fixing them before observation and preserving them throughout the study."}]}, {"id": 5, "heading": "Limitations and Conclusion", "original": "The study is small and focuses on a short observation period. Even a clear difference in growth would not directly demonstrate cellular damage [S1]. The design also does not test whether seedlings recover after salt is removed [S2]. Those questions would need additional measurements and a different follow-up period rather than stronger wording about the same observations.", "candidate": "The study is small and limited to a short observation period. Even a clear difference in growth would not directly demonstrate cellular damage [S1]. Additionally, the design does not test whether seedlings recover after salt is removed [S2]. To address these questions, further measurements and a different follow-up period would be necessary.", "issues": [{"originalQuote": "Those questions would need additional measurements and a different follow-up period rather than stronger wording about the same observations.", "revisedQuote": "To address these questions, further measurements and a different follow-up period would be necessary.", "problem": "The revision omits the explicit interpretive limitation that stronger wording about the existing observations cannot answer these questions."}]}], "sources": [{"id": "S1", "title": "Controlled source packet: domain and evidence brief", "excerpt": "The planned plant study compares seedlings under salt treatment with a water-only control. The treatment is 40 millimolar salt; the control contains no added salt. Height and leaf colour are observations, not direct measures of cellular damage. The proposal contains no completed experimental findings.", "content_kind": "author_constructed_evaluation_fixture"}, {"id": "S2", "title": "Controlled source packet: experimental design brief", "excerpt": "There will be 30 seedlings in each condition, observed for 12 days. The primary comparison is change in height, with leaf colour as a secondary observation. Plants that fail to grow will remain in the analysis. The design does not test recovery after treatment removal.", "content_kind": "author_constructed_evaluation_fixture"}]}
